/-!
# Presentations (port of `present.v`)

Coq's `present.v` defines the properties used by the unavoidability proof (`reducibility`,
`valid_hub`, `excluded_arity`, `successful`, `forced_part`, `succeeds_in`), the lemmas behind
each step of a presentation, and a scripting language (tactic notations) in which the seven
presentation lemmas `exclude5` … `exclude11` (`present5.v` … `present11.v`) are written. The
Lean port keeps the definitions and lemmas, and replaces the scripting language by data: a case
tree `PTree`, checked by the kernel with `checkTree`, whose soundness is proved once.

* `FourColor.Present.Basic`: the definitions and the lemmas of `present.v`, and their variants
  with the fast checks of `FourColor.Fast` (a pruned quiz tree, any drule fork).
* `FourColor.Present.Tree`: the case trees `PTree`, the goals `PGoal`, the checker `checkTree`,
  its soundness `checkTree_sound`, and the composition lemmas for presentations split into
  chunks (`PGoal.ok_of_checkTree`, `excludedArity_of_ok`, `excludedArity_of_checkTree`,
  `PGoal.ok_of_hubcap`).

The presentation data (the trees of `present5.v` … `present11.v`, with the pruning masks of
their leaves, split into chunk theorems) is generated by `scripts/present_gen.py` under
`FourColor/Present/P5/` … `FourColor/Present/P11/`, whose `Exclude` modules prove `exclude5` …
`exclude11`; `FourColor/Unavoidability.lean` collates them.

